The '''World Research Conference''' is a recurring international scientific conference that brings together researchers from across [[Adonia]] to present and discuss advances in the physical and natural sciences. Modeled on the principle of open international scientific exchange, the conference convenes at rotating host institutions in different Adonian countries.

The conference is regarded as one of the most significant forums for scientific communication in Adonia. Major discoveries and theoretical advances have been presented at the conference, including the [[discovery of nuclear fission]] by [[Tân Bûn-kong]] and [[Lîm Chiat-bêng]] at the 1933 edition in [[Ampuria]], [[Volisania]].

== Notable editions ==

=== 1933 — Ampuria, Volisania ===

{{main|Discovery of nuclear fission}}

The 1933 edition, held in [[Ampuria]], [[Volisania]], is the most historically significant edition of the conference. [[Tân Bûn-kong]] and [[Lîm Chiat-bêng]] presented the results of their 1932 experiments at the [[University of Anping]], announcing the [[discovery of nuclear fission]] to the international scientific community. The presentation generated immediate interest, and several national delegations returned to their home countries to replicate the experiments, confirming the Anping results within months.

The choice of Ampuria as host reflected the city's status as a major centre of learning, home to the [[University of Ampuria]], one of the oldest universities in Volisania.

